    <description>The 1.23-meter Telescope is an optical telescope located at Calar Alto Observatory in Spain. It was originally part of a collaboration between NASA and the Max Planck Institute for Astronomy. With a 1.23-meter primary mirror, it has been used for a variety of astronomical observations, including studies of asteroids, comets, stars, and galaxies. The telescope has also supported planetary defense initiatives by tracking near-Earth objects.
